  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Cli\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Cli\n       Program: commons-cli\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Cli/Cli.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-cli.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Cli/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 39\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Cli-7\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\n4ee0d6c4f1b553858aeabf3ee6fb37d764f263e2\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2008-02-21 08:03:23 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nCLI-121\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CLI-121\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.cli2.bug.Bug27575Test::testRequiredOptions\n   --> junit.framework.ComparisonFailure: expected:<[[-h]]> but was:<[-c <arg>]>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.cli2.builder.PatternBuilder\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: Tests fail under 1.6 + error at end that may or may not be related\nType: Bug | Priority: Major | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nTestsuite: org.apache.commons.cli2.bug.Bug27575Test\nTests run: 1, Failures: 1, Errors: 0, Time elapsed: 0.058 sec\n\nTestcase: testRequiredOptions(org.apache.commons.cli2.bug.Bug27575Test):        FAILED\nexpected:<[-h]> but was:<-c <arg>>\njunit.framework.ComparisonFailure: expected:<[-h]> but was:<-c <arg>>\n        at org.apache.commons.cli2.bug.Bug27575Test.testRequiredOptions(Bug27575Test.java:36)\n        at sun.reflect.NativeMethodAccessorImpl.invoke0(Native Method)\n        at sun.reflect.NativeMethodAccessorImpl.invoke(NativeMethodAccessorImpl.java:39)\n\n\nand error at end of:\n\nException in thread \"Thread-1\" javax.xml.transform.TransformerFactoryConfigurationError: Provider for javax.xml.transform.TransformerFactory cannot be found\n        at javax.xml.transform.TransformerFactory.newInstance(Unknown Source)\n        at java.util.prefs.XmlSupport.writeDoc(XmlSupport.java:246)\n        at java.util.prefs.XmlSupport.exportMap(XmlSupport.java:333)\n        at java.util.prefs.FileSystemPreferences$8.run(FileSystemPreferences.java:607)\n\nComments:\n\n[Henri Yandell]: Given the timeline of the JDK, I think this should be solved in 2.0 if possible.\n\n[Oliver Heger]: PatternBuilder used to store all defined options in a set, so there is no guarantee for the order, in which they are returned. Obviously an implementation change between JDK 1.5 and 1.6 produces a different order and causes this test to fail.\n\nThe attached patch changes PatternBuilder to use a LinkedHashSet instead, which keeps the order of created options. (Alternatively the test could be changed so that it does not force a certain order, but I think the order, in which options are defined by PatternBuilder may be important anyway.)\n\nNote that LinkedHashSet is available in JDK 1.4+ only. Which are the JDK requirements for CLI2?\n\nI cannot reproduce the other error related to a XML configuration.\n\n[Sebb]: Perhaps use Commons Collections ListOrderedSet to get round the Java 1.4 restriction if required?\n\n[Oliver Heger]: Using ListOrderedSet would be an alternative, but this would mean another dependency. CLI2 does not depend on commons collections so far.\n\n[Henri Yandell]: I don't see any reason not to be JDK 1.4+, so +1 to using LinkedHashSet.",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.cli2.builder.PatternBuilder (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.cli2.builder.PatternBuilder (fixed)\n@@ -16,8 +16,8 @@\n  */\n package org.apache.commons.cli2.builder;\n \n-import java.util.HashSet;\n import java.util.Iterator;\n+import java.util.LinkedHashSet;\n import java.util.Set;\n \n import org.apache.commons.cli2.Argument;\n@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@\n         this.abuilder = abuilder;\n     }\n \n-    private final Set options = new HashSet();\n+    private final Set options = new LinkedHashSet();\n \n     /**\n      * Creates a new Option instance."
